WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.600
So one of the biggest, um, dividing lines
we could call it

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.870
the American left and right, is about what
role should government have in our lives.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.990
How big should government be, what are the
things that government should and shouldn't

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:21.279
be doing? And the public policy mood estimate
is a measure of exactly that. And it is at

00:00:21.279 --> 00:00:27.449
the most liberal point in the 68 year history
of the measure. And it's really important

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:32.090
to understand that this measure doesn't address
the public's view on a lot of the issues that

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.910
have been big parts of the Donald Trump administration.
So immigration is not addressed by the public

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:44.940
policy mood report. Um, trade is not in any
way addressed by this. It's specifically related

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.280
to the role and scope of government in society.
And I have to tell you the results are not

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.860
actually very surprising because when we look
at individual issue polls where people are

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.310
asked, should the government provide a basic
level of healthcare to everybody, regardless

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:04.440
of whether they can pay for it, the country
is the most to the left that it has been on

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.440
that issue.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.920
People, by and large thinking, the answer
is yes. The government should provide some

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.979
basic level of care to everybody even if they
can't pay for it. And part of the reason why

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:20.630
is that whether your sim sympathies to that
idea are ideological or moral or economic,

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:25.819
we now realize that hey, we're a well rich
enough country that we can be making sure

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:30.289
everybody has a basic level of care and it's
also good economically because when people

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:35.119
have access to health care, all sorts of other
negative externalities are mitigated like

00:01:35.119 --> 00:01:41.049
work, absenteeism and productivity. If that
is what you care about or criminality related

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:45.749
to needing money to pay for medical treatments,
medical bankruptcies, all of that stuff. Whatever

00:01:45.749 --> 00:01:51.709
your sympathies are with regards to healthcare,
more and more of the country now recognizes

00:01:51.709 --> 00:01:56.810
everybody's better off. If the government
does something that we can very easily afford

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:02.819
to do, which is make sure everybody has some
basic level of care on the issue of taxation.

00:02:02.819 --> 00:02:08.630
Should the government be using taxation to
reduce income inequality? By taxing the very,

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:13.810
very rich, the country has moved to the left
on that. It has been a significant and steady

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:18.750
move to the left. Now I know that there are
still people who don't want, uh, the rich

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.760
to be taxed. I know there are still people
who believe that it's not good economically

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:28.220
to tax the very, very rich to lift the bottom
end and make sure nobody gets left behind.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.440
You can find those people. Many of them voted
for Trump, but in total the country has moved

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.370
to the left in terms of believing that that
is a role that government should be playing.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:45.110
This is why Republicans don't want people
to vote. When you understand and recognize

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:50.470
that on the issues, the country is well to
the left of our elected officials. You don't

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.640
want people to vote.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.830
The ideas that people have come around to,
and this is bigger than Trump, are more or

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:03.280
less the ideas of Franklin d Roosevelt. Second
Bill of rights. FDR proposed this during his

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:10.170
1944 state of the Union address, the con,
the elements of it were employment of bill

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:14.880
of rights that contains employment, meaning
the right to work, food, clothing and leisure

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:20.061
with enough income to support those activities.
Uh, farmers, right to a fair income. This

00:03:20.061 --> 00:03:25.530
was very important in the u s at the time,
freedom from unfair competition and monopolies.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:32.170
Elizabeth Warren is talking about this housing,
medical care, social security and education.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:39.950
This is from 1944 I would add to the second
bill of rights, um, now protecting the environment

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:45.440
in the context of the climate crisis that
we're facing. But this is all about government's

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:52.050
role and on government's role in total. The
country is as le left as it has ever been.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:56.840
So if we fix our election system, we might
actually have a shot at making more of these

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:02.690
things a reality because the most liberal
public mood ever is not going to get progressive

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:08.540
politicians elected if we don't fix campaign
finance, if we don't fix the election systems,

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:14.790
if we don't stop voter suppression. This does
also relate, by the way to my story yesterday,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.590
pointing out that Donald Trump is mostly the
result of decades of right wing anti intellectual

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:27.440
Elysium and demonization of progressive ideas.
But Donald Trump's rise to power is also partially

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:34.500
a result of milk, toast, centrist, status
quo ideas from corporate democrats for much

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:40.090
of that same multi-decade periods. So all
these issues with campaign finance and voting

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:46.840
systems do need to be fixed. But Democrats
also need to get with it and move to the left.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:52.070
As some Democratic candidates for 2020 are
finally starting to do as some members of

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:55.490
the Progressive House caucus are finally starting
to do.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:59.100
There's plenty of blame to go around. It's
not everybody is equally to blame, but when

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:04.230
you understand that on the issues, the American
public has moved to the left, it immediately

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:07.389
becomes obvious why Republicans have been
behaving the way they've been behaving when

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:12.290
it comes to who is allowed to vote, what is
required to vote, what are the number of places

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:17.740
that people are allowed to vote and why do
they want to reduce that? And they have, uh,

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:22.669
sporadically gone public and made it clear.
Remember that guy, I think his name was Mike

00:05:22.669 --> 00:05:30.040
Turzai who said, uh, voter ID will deliver
Pennsylvania to Mitt Romney. They understand

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:36.310
this. Okay. They're willing to play dirty
and to a great extent, they have secured numerous,

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.630
endless election victories as a result of
their willingness to do it. You Democrats

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.090
need to stoop to the same level. Well, it's
not stooping when you try to get more people

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.090
to vote.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:50.180
Okay. That's called the spirit of democracy
and we need to understand all of these elements.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:54.710
It's fantastic that the country is moving
left. We just need to make it possible for

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:59.360
that leftward move to be reflected in the
elected officials that we put into power and

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:04.560
voter suppression, voter Id, reducing voting
hours, reducing polling places, all of that

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:09.000
is going to make it harder for the will of
the people, which is more left than ever to

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.080
actually be made a reality.

